# Build
/target

# Configuration locale (utiliser config.example.toml comme modèle)
/config.toml

# Captures / dumps éventuels
/captures
*.bin

# Notes internes — ne jamais publier
/info.txt
/BOT_COORDINATES.md
/UI_LAYER_REFERENCE.md

# Divers OS / éditeur
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Instructions agent — local, jamais publié
/CLAUDE.md

# Plans d'amélioration et worktrees d'agents — local, jamais commité
/plans
/.claude

# Runtime panic log (crash.log; app-data first, temp-dir fallback)
crash.log

# Packet captures. The capture backend is Npcap (see src/capture/pcap), and a
# manual debugging session — dumping with Wireshark/dumpcap or exporting a
# capture from it — writes a `.pcap`/`.pcapng` next to wherever it was run,
# which is often the repo root. `.etl` stays too: Windows' built-in tracing
# (Event Trace Log) produces the same hazard through a different tool. These
# hold real network traffic and must never reach a commit.
*.etl
*.pcap
*.pcapng
